Fixed date-times with a ``TZID`` that names a time zone equivalent to UTC, such as ``Etc/UTC`` or ``GMT``, being written with both the ``TZID`` and a ``Z`` suffix, which :rfc:`5545#section-3.3.5` forbids. In iCalendar output, such a date-time is now written in UTC, without the ``TZID``. This was a regression in 6.1.3. I used Claude Opus 5.5 to bisect the regression, write the tests and the fix. @tobixen
